/* Symbols that must not be re-exported from the OCCT shared libraries, passed to ld as
 * --version-script (Linux). The Mach-O counterpart is deps/occt-unexported-symbols.txt.
 *
 * FreeType is linked statically into libTKService and would otherwise re-export ~220 FT_* symbols. ELF has one
 * flat namespace, so a process that loads another FreeType -- matplotlib, Pillow and Qt all bundle one -- can
 * bind OCCT's calls to that one instead (CadQuery/ocp-build-system#54). On Linux the second copy is not even
 * hypothetical: libTKService needs libfontconfig.so.1, whose own DT_NEEDED names libfreetype.so.6, so OCCT
 * puts a second FreeType in the process by itself.
 *
 * Until 2026-09-25 this was done by patching FreeType's own header (deps/hide-freetype-symbols.sh, removed):
 * the same effect, but it modified a dependency, which has to be re-checked at every bump and declared in
 * NOTICE as a modified copy. Doing it at link time leaves the dependency pristine.
 *
 * "global: *" keeps everything else exported -- OCCT's own API is what these libraries are for. Only the
 * patterns under "local:" are hidden. Measured against the unpatched static libfreetype.a: FT_*, FTC_* and
 * TT_* and nothing else.
 *
 * FreeImage needs nothing here: it is a shared library built with -fvisibility=hidden, so it exports only its
 * own FreeImage_* API and none of its bundled codecs (deps/build-freeimage-manylinux.sh).
 */
{
  global: *;
  local:
    FT_*;
    FTC_*;
    TT_*;
};
